@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:deployment] updater-candidate-identity
The updater MUST build one fixed Git revision with committed locks, as that
revision's //fleet/hosts/<host>:deployment Buck2 target (ADR-0271; it was the
nixosConfigurations attribute), use that candidate's secret descriptors and
migrator, and activate exactly the system closure the target reports. Only successful activation followed by bounded role health checks, or
verification of an identical already-active system and manifest, may advance
lastHealthy. Every candidate secret-preparation service MUST also be
active before marking a deployment healthy, including when its unit definition
is unchanged. No updater path may automatically roll back database state.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] updater-private-staging
Secret staging MUST remain root-only and separate from live bundles until
compatibility and migrations succeed. Process arguments, status and journals
MUST exclude secret values. Existing consumers MUST stop before bundle changes.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] updater-guest-and-identity-preservation
Updates MUST preserve enrolled Lilly identity bindings and independently supervised
guests. Reviewed ADR-0050 resource tuning MAY increase guest CPU/RAM/quota limits
in place and change the ARC target. The updater MUST NOT open a competing Lilly session, rotate authority,
format storage, reboot, or destroy unrelated checkout/state paths.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] updater-socket-activation-order
Declared socket activators MUST stop before their consumers during activation
and return to their prior active state afterward. A failed activation MUST
attempt to restore the consumer roles that were active before stopping them.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] updater-installation-binding
Ordinary updates MUST reject installationBinding changes except ADR-0050's exact
quota allowlist, verified against unchanged native GUIDs and journaled original
receipts. Removal, introduction and topology/identity changes require maintenance.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] updater-effective-protected-networks
The Lilly binding comparison MUST treat protectedCidrs plus readable runtime
protected address files as one effective set. Unreadable or malformed runtime
files MUST fail closed to raw comparison.
